{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2158-12-15 11:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning, Ms. ___ . I'm Dr. ___ , part of the surgical team. You're here today for a planned procedure on your left arm fistula because of the hand pain and numbness you've been having during dialysis."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2158-12-15 11:31:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, thank you. It really hurts when the blood flow goes above 300. My hand gets cold and tingly. I was hoping this would fix it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2158-12-15 11:32:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s exactly what we call steal syndrome — the fistula is pulling too much blood away from your hand. Today, we’ll do a banding procedure to reduce the flow and see if that helps."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2158-12-15 11:33:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, that makes sense. Will I be asleep?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2158-12-15 11:34:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ll be under light sedation and local anesthesia. It’s a minimally invasive procedure, so recovery is usually quick."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2158-12-15 11:35:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my warfarin? I take it every other day."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2158-12-15 11:36:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ve held your warfarin starting today. Since you’re on anticoagulants, we’ll use a heparin drip to keep your blood thin enough during the hospital stay, especially around the procedure."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2158-12-15 11:37:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, as long as my valve is protected."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2158-12-15 11:38:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Exactly. Your mechanical valve means you need consistent anticoagulation, so we’ll manage that carefully. We’ll restart warfarin once your INR is back in range."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2158-12-15 12:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi again. The banding procedure went smoothly. You tolerated it well, and there were no complications."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2158-12-15 12:31:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s good. But my hand still feels numb. Is that normal?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2158-12-15 12:32:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It is concerning. We still can’t feel your radial pulse, and the numbness hasn’t gone away. That suggests the banding didn’t fully fix the steal. We’ll need to do a fistulagram to see what’s going on."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2158-12-15 12:33:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Another test? What is that?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2158-12-15 12:34:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It’s a special X-ray where we inject contrast into your fistula to see the blood flow. It’ll show us exactly where the problem is."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2158-12-15 12:35:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’m allergic to IV dye, though."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2158-12-15 12:36:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ve noted that. We’ll use a low-iodine contrast and pre-medicate you to reduce the risk. It’s important we get this image to plan the next step."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2158-12-16 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. You had dialysis yesterday, and I wanted to check in. How’s your hand feeling?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2158-12-16 10:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Worse, actually. During dialysis, the numbness came back, and my fingers felt even colder."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2158-12-16 10:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That confirms our concern. The fistulagram is scheduled for tomorrow. It looks like the banding didn’t reduce the steal enough. We may need to revise the fistula."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2158-12-16 10:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Revise it how?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2158-12-16 10:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Possibly reroute the blood flow or use a vein graft to redirect some flow back to your hand. The imaging will help us decide."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2158-12-17 14:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi. The fistulagram showed persistent steal. Blood is still being pulled too strongly through the fistula. We’re scheduling you for surgery to revise it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2158-12-17 14:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Another surgery? How soon?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2158-12-17 14:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Day after tomorrow — day after tomorrow. We need to map some veins first to see if we can use one as a graft."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2158-12-18 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We did vein mapping today. The left cephalic vein is usable, and we’ll harvest it to create a new pathway. The plan is to redirect flow from the radial artery to improve hand circulation."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2158-12-18 09:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So it’s like building a detour?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2158-12-18 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Exactly. We’ll reduce the steal and restore blood flow to your hand."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2158-12-19 13:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi. You’re back from surgery. The revision went well. We used your cephalic vein to create a new connection and explored the radial artery. You’re doing fine."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2158-12-19 13:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "My hand feels warmer already. The tingling is gone."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2158-12-19 13:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s excellent. We can feel your radial pulse now, which means blood is flowing back to your hand. That’s a great sign."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2158-12-20 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. You had dialysis yesterday with full blood flow — 400 cc/min — and no symptoms. That’s a big improvement."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2158-12-20 08:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I didn’t feel any pain or numbness. I could actually feel my fingers!"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2158-12-20 08:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s exactly what we wanted. Your hand is getting the blood it needs now."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2158-12-20 08:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "What about my warfarin?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2158-12-20 08:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We restarted your warfarin two days ago. Your INR was low, so we kept the heparin drip going. Now that your INR is rising, we’ll stop the heparin soon."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2158-12-21 07:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your INR is now 2.6 — that’s in the therapeutic range. We’ve turned off the heparin drip. You’re fully anticoagulated again."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2158-12-21 07:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Good. I was worried about my heart valve."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2158-12-21 07:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re monitoring closely. You’ve stayed on your regular dialysis schedule and medications, and you’ve had no other issues."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2158-12-22 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Just checking in. How’s the incision site?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2158-12-22 09:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "It’s a little sore, but no redness or drainage. I’ve been keeping it dry like you said."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2158-12-22 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good. Remember — no blood pressures or lab draws from that arm. And no lifting more than 10 pounds."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2158-12-22 09:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I won’t. I’ll be careful."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2158-12-23 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re planning for discharge in a couple of days. You’ve healed well, and your hand function has returned."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2158-12-23 10:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s great. What do I need to do at home?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2158-12-23 10:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Continue dialysis as scheduled. Check your fistula daily for the buzzing — that’s the thrill. If it’s gone, call the access clinic right away."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 46,
      "time": "2158-12-23 10:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And if my hand gets cold again?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 47,
      "time": "2158-12-23 10:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That could be a sign of steal returning. Call immediately if you have pain, coldness, blue fingers, or numbness."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 48,
      "time": "2158-12-24 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your INR is stable. We’ve arranged for your next lab draw during your dialysis session."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 49,
      "time": "2158-12-24 08:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my warfarin dose?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 50,
      "time": "2158-12-24 08:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ll take 6 mg daily for two days, then go back to your usual every-other-day schedule based on the lab results."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 51,
      "time": "2158-12-25 07:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re doing so well. We’re finalizing discharge for tomorrow."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 52,
      "time": "2158-12-25 07:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’m ready to go home. Thank you for fixing my hand."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 53,
      "time": "2158-12-26 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll discharge you tomorrow morning. Just a few final instructions."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 54,
      "time": "2158-12-26 09:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, I’m listening."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 55,
      "time": "2158-12-26 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Keep the incision clean and dry. No soaking — just gentle washing. Cover it if there’s any drainage."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 56,
      "time": "2158-12-26 09:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Got it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 57,
      "time": "2158-12-26 09:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "No tight clothes or jewelry on that arm. And continue all your home meds, diet, and fluid limits."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 58,
      "time": "2158-12-26 09:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. I’ve been doing that for years."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 59,
      "time": "2158-12-27 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. You’re cleared to go home today."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 60,
      "time": "2158-12-27 08:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Finally! I feel so much better."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 61,
      "time": "2158-12-27 08:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your hand is healing well, the steal is resolved, and your anticoagulation is stable."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 62,
      "time": "2158-12-27 08:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you. I’ll call if anything changes."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 63,
      "time": "2158-12-27 08:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Exactly. And keep up with your follow-up labs and dialysis. You’re doing great."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 64,
      "time": "2158-12-27 08:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. Thanks again, Doctor."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 65,
      "time": "2158-12-27 08:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Take care, and we’ll see you in the access clinic if needed."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2158-12-15 11:15:00",
    "admission_end": "2158-12-27 16:33:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "A woman with end-stage renal disease on hemodialysis was admitted for elective banding of her left brachiocephalic arteriovenous fistula due to steal syndrome causing hand pain, numbness, and poor perfusion. After initial banding failed to resolve symptoms, a fistulagram confirmed ongoing steal, leading to a revision surgery involving cephalic vein harvest and reconfiguration of flow from the radial artery. Postoperatively, her symptoms resolved, radial pulse returned, and she tolerated full-dose dialysis without issues. Anticoagulation was managed with heparin drip during warfarin hold, then transitioned back to warfarin as INR reached therapeutic levels. She was discharged home in stable condition with detailed instructions on access site care, anticoagulation management, and when to seek urgent care.",
    "problems": [
      "Other complications due to renal dialysis device, implant, and graft",
      "End stage renal disease",
      "Complications of transplanted kidney",
      "Hypertensive chronic kidney disease, unspecified, with chronic kidney disease stage V or end stage renal disease",
      "Chronic diastolic heart failure",
      "Congestive heart failure, unspecified",
      "Surgical operation with anastomosis, bypass, or graft, with natural or artificial tissues used as implant causing abnormal patient reaction, or later complication, without mention of misadventure at time of operation",
      "Renal dialysis status",
      "Coronary atherosclerosis of unspecified type of vessel, native or graft",
      "Aortocoronary bypass status",
      "Percutaneous transluminal coronary angioplasty status",
      "Automatic implantable cardiac defibrillator in situ",
      "Heart valve replaced by other means",
      "Personal history of tobacco use",
      "Personal history of transient ischemic attack (TIA), and cerebral infarction without residual deficits",
      "Hyperpotassemia",
      "Acquired absence of kidney",
      "Surgical operation with transplant of whole organ causing abnormal patient reaction, or later complication, without mention of misadventure at time of operation"
    ]
  }
}
